    "https://floridatech.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/FloridaTechCareers/job/Florida-Tech-Main-Campus-Melbourne/Dispatcher_R9707": {
      "title": "Dispatcher",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-07\nFull time\n\nThe Department of Security Dispatchers' responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Assisting students and campus employees via the phone, email, and in person. As well as the ability to respond appropriately to 911 or non-emergency numbers. Dispatchers also provide administrative support and must be able to perform a range of secondary administrative and clerical duties. The ideal candidate should have excellent oral and written communication skills, experience in Microsoft Word and Excel, and the ability to remain calm and in control within a busy professional workplace. Department of Security Dispatchers work within a 24-hour, 7-day-a-week operation and, due to the nature of the position, are expected to work an 80-hour pay cycle with a fluctuating schedule that includes holidays, nights, and weekends. Answer multiple phone lines and dispatch officers to appropriate locations on and off campus using a two-way radio for daily calls and emergency situations. Assists walk-ins with their inquiries in accordance with established procedures. Provide safety awareness through daily contact with the university community and visitors by providing general safety information, directions, and parking information. Dispatch officers to all emergencies, coordinate law enforcement, medical, and /or fire assistance, provide a proactive role after the emergency, and make appropriate notifications on campus as directed. Utilize the Computer Aided Dispatch (CAD) system as appropriate. Provide clerical support as needed, special projects, scanning, and data entry. May be required to work during emergencies, which may require the dispatcher to remain at the university until the emergency has terminated. Work designated alternate hours and perform other responsibilities as needed. Other duties as assigned.   Experience/Skills: Administrative experience, dispatch experience, proficiency in Microsoft Office (Excel and Word), and familiarity with our industry are preferred. Security, military, law enforcement, correctional, medical, dispatch, and/or administrative support experience is favored.    Equal Opportunity Florida Institute of Technology does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national or ethnic origin, religion, disability, age, genetic information, marital status, citizenship status, veteran status, and other legally protected characteristics in its activities and programs. In accordance with Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Florida Tech does not discriminate on the basis of sex.  Inquiries concerning the application of the Non-Discrimination and Anti-Harassment policy may be directed to the Equal Opportunity Director and Investigator at 150 West University Blvd, Melbourne, FL 32901, or email equalopp@fit.edu , or +1 321-674-7153; or to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Americans with Disabilities Act Please notify us at least five days in advance if a reasonable accommodation for a disability is needed by calling the Office of Human Resources at 321-674-8100. Annual Security & Fire Safety Report The federal Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act (Clery Act) requires colleges and universities, both public and private, participating in federal student aid programs to disclose campus safety information, and imposes certain basic requirements for handling incidents of sexual violence and emergency situations. Florida Tech’s 2026 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report includes statistics for the previous three years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus; in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by Florida Tech; and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from, the campus.   The numbers provided include crime statistics that were reported to local law enforcement agencies, campus security and other Campus Security Authorities.   The report also includes institutional policy statements regarding campus safety and security measures; descriptions of prevention and awareness programs; related university procedures and important guidance; and other essential safety information. You can obtain a printed copy of this report at the Department of Security Welcome Center located at 3126 Panther Place, during normal business hours, or by accessing the following web site 2026 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report . Official Transcripts Official transcripts of all collegiate work must be sent directly from the attended institution to the Office of Human Resources prior to the first day of employment. All international degrees must have a course-by-course official evaluation and translation sent to the Human Resources Office directly from an evaluation company affiliated with the National Association of Credential Evaluation Services, Inc. (NACES). We are an E-verify employer"
    },
    "https://floridatech.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/FloridaTechCareers/job/Florida-Tech-Main-Campus-Melbourne/Senior-Contract-Specialist-and-Export-Control-Officer_R9705": {
      "title": "Senior Contract Specialist and Export Control Officer",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-07\nFull time\n\nThe Senior Contract Specialist and Export Control Officer (SCSECO) is responsible for managing a comprehensive pre-award portfolio and supporting the University's research administration, contracting, export control, and secure research compliance activities. This position serves as a key resource for faculty, staff, and administrators in the development and submission of externally funded proposals, as well as the review and negotiation of research-related agreements. The SCSECO assists principal investigators with all aspects of proposal development and submission, including interpretation of sponsor guidelines, proposal budget development and review, completion of sponsor-required forms, certifications and assurances, collection of subrecipient documentation, and review of proposal packages for accuracy, completeness, and compliance with sponsor and institutional requirements. The position ensures the timely completion of internal approvals and assists with the submission of proposals to federal, state, industry, and foundation sponsors. The SCSECO reviews, negotiates, and facilitates the execution of research-related agreements, including sponsored research agreements, industry and government contracts, non-disclosure agreements, memoranda of understanding, material transfer agreements, teaming agreements, data use agreements, and other research-related documents. This role works closely with institutional leadership, legal counsel, and sponsoring organizations to clarify terms and conditions and ensure consistency with university policies and applicable federal, state, and local regulations. The position researches and applies relevant laws, regulations, sponsor requirements, and institutional policies related to sponsored programs, contracting, export controls, and research security. Responsibilities include supporting the University's Export Control Program and assisting with compliance requirements related to Controlled Unclassified Information (CUI), research security, foreign influence and disclosure requirements, technology control plans, restricted research, and other federal regulations governing sensitive and secure research activities. The SCSECO provides guidance and training to faculty and staff regarding export control, research security, and sponsor compliance requirements and assists with institutional efforts to expand participation in secure and government-sponsored research programs. This is not a remote position. Job Responsibilities - Assist in maintaining a secure research environment for FTRI by supporting compliance with Controlled Unclassified Information (CUI) requirements, technology control plans, sponsor security requirements, and other federal regulations governing sensitive, restricted, and classified research. - Assist faculty, administrators, & staff with proposal preparation & submission; review sponsor requirements; develop & negotiate award terms & conditions; secure required institutional approvals; coordinate with principal investigators, departments, & sponsors to ensure compliance and process award modifications, budget revisions, & NCEs. - Assist with the export control duties to ensure its industry, research and scholarly activities are conducted in compliance with the US export control laws and regulations, and monitor the university's conflict of interest program. - Work with the principal investigators, department administrators and the sponsors during the term of the award to ensure compliance with grant terms. Submit requests for modification, no-cost extensions, budget revisions and other activities. - Develop, negotiate, and maintain various agreements, including but not limited to sponsored research agreements (e.g. master agreements, SBIRs/STTRs, and subawards), confidentiality, material transfer, collaboration, and teaming agreements. - Research and apply rules, laws, and policies concerning higher education contracts. Assist with the development and implementation of Sponsored Program Policies and Procedures and research compliance policies and procedures (export controls, COI, RCR, etc.) that are consistent with Federal and State laws. Requirements: Bachelor’s degree (or equivalent knowledge obtained through a combination of education, training and experience) Minimum 5–8 years of experience required in area of expertise Preferred Certifications : Certified Research Administrator (CRA), Certified Export Compliance Professional (CECP), Certified Compliance & Ethics Professional (CCEP), Certified Information Systems Security Professional (CISSP) (preferred for secure research environments), NCURA Research Security Certificate, NCURA Export Controls Certificate Preferred Skills : Uniform Guidance 2 CFR 200, ITAR, EAR, OFAC sanctions regulations, deemed export requirements, foreign national participation reviews, restricted party screening, NPSM-33 requirements, CHIPS and Science Act research security provisions, foreign influence and foreign talent program regulations, research security training requirements, DoE, DoD, NSF, and NIH security mandates. CUI categorization and marking requirements, controlled environment requirements, data handling and safeguarding procedures, incident reporting requirements, Technology Control Plans (TCPs), establishing secure research environments, conducting facility and project security reviews. Equal Opportunity Florida Institute of Technology does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national or ethnic origin, religion, disability, age, genetic information, marital status, citizenship status, veteran status, and other legally protected characteristics in its activities and programs. In accordance with Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Florida Tech does not discriminate on the basis of sex.  Inquiries concerning the application of the Non-Discrimination and Anti-Harassment policy may be directed to the Equal Opportunity Director and Investigator at 150 West University Blvd, Melbourne, FL 32901, or email equalopp@fit.edu , or +1 321-674-7153; or to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Americans with Disabilities Act Please notify us at least five days in advance if a reasonable accommodation for a disability is needed by calling the Office of Human Resources at 321-674-8100. Annual Security & Fire Safety Report The federal Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act (Clery Act) requires colleges and universities, both public and private, participating in federal student aid programs to disclose campus safety information, and imposes certain basic requirements for handling incidents of sexual violence and emergency situations. Florida Tech’s 2026 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report includes statistics for the previous three years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus; in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by Florida Tech; and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from, the campus.   The numbers provided include crime statistics that were reported to local law enforcement agencies, campus security and other Campus Security Authorities.   The report also includes institutional policy statements regarding campus safety and security measures; descriptions of prevention and awareness programs; related university procedures and important guidance; and other essential safety information. You can obtain a printed copy of this report at the Department of Security Welcome Center located at 3126 Panther Place, during normal business hours, or by accessing the following web site 2026 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report . Official Transcripts Official transcripts of all collegiate work must be sent directly from the attended institution to the Office of Human Resources prior to the first day of employment. All international degrees must have a course-by-course official evaluation and translation sent to the Human Resources Office directly from an evaluation company affiliated with the National Association of Credential Evaluation Services, Inc. (NACES). We are an E-verify employer"
    },
    "https://floridatech.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/FloridaTechCareers/job/Florida-Tech-Main-Campus-Melbourne/Contract-Specialist-and-Grant-Administrator_R9706": {
      "title": "Contract Specialist and Grant Administrator",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-06\nFull time\n\nThe Contract Specialist and Grants Administrator provides comprehensive support for sponsored programs administration with primary responsibilities in proposal development, award administration, and research-related agreement management. This position serves as a resource to faculty and staff throughout the lifecycle of sponsored projects by assisting with proposal preparation, contract administration, compliance requirements, award modifications, and institutional reporting while ensuring adherence to sponsor and university requirements. - Review, process, route, & coordinate research-related agreements, including non-disclosure agreements, memoranda of understanding, material transfer agreements, & other research-related documents. Maintain records & workflows within the University's contract management system (Cayuse) & coordinate with stakeholders to facilitate timely execution. - Assist faculty & staff with proposal preparation/submission activities, including interpretation of sponsor guidelines, budget development/review, preparation of sponsor-required forms, certifications, assurances, collection of required documentation, & review of proposal packages to ensure compliance with sponsor & institutional requirements. - Support post-award administration activities by coordinating award modifications, no-cost extensions, budget revisions, prior approval requests, and other sponsor-required actions. Maintain proposal, award, and agreement records and assist with ensuring compliance with sponsor and university policies and procedures. - Provide administrative support to the Office of Sponsored Research by responding to inquiries, preparing correspondence, maintaining files, scheduling meetings, coordinating documentation, and supporting special projects. - Prepare reports, metrics, and other information related to sponsored projects, proposals, agreements, and research administration activities. Assist with the development, implementation, and communication of sponsored programs policies, procedures, training materials, and best practices. - Perform other duties as assigned. Equal Opportunity Florida Institute of Technology does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national or ethnic origin, religion, disability, age, genetic information, marital status, citizenship status, veteran status, and other legally protected characteristics in its activities and programs. In accordance with Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Florida Tech does not discriminate on the basis of sex.  Inquiries concerning the application of the Non-Discrimination and Anti-Harassment policy may be directed to the Equal Opportunity Director and Investigator at 150 West University Blvd, Melbourne, FL 32901, or email equalopp@fit.edu , or +1 321-674-7153; or to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Americans with Disabilities Act Please notify us at least five days in advance if a reasonable accommodation for a disability is needed by calling the Office of Human Resources at 321-674-8100. Annual Security & Fire Safety Report The federal Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act (Clery Act) requires colleges and universities, both public and private, participating in federal student aid programs to disclose campus safety information, and imposes certain basic requirements for handling incidents of sexual violence and emergency situations. Florida Tech’s 2026 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report includes statistics for the previous three years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus; in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by Florida Tech; and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from, the campus.   The numbers provided include crime statistics that were reported to local law enforcement agencies, campus security and other Campus Security Authorities.   The report also includes institutional policy statements regarding campus safety and security measures; descriptions of prevention and awareness programs; related university procedures and important guidance; and other essential safety information. You can obtain a printed copy of this report at the Department of Security Welcome Center located at 3126 Panther Place, during normal business hours, or by accessing the following web site 2026 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report . Official Transcripts Official transcripts of all collegiate work must be sent directly from the attended institution to the Office of Human Resources prior to the first day of employment. All international degrees must have a course-by-course official evaluation and translation sent to the Human Resources Office directly from an evaluation company affiliated with the National Association of Credential Evaluation Services, Inc. (NACES). We are an E-verify employer"
    },
    "https://floridatech.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/FloridaTechCareers/job/Florida-Tech-Main-Campus-Melbourne/WBC-Program-Coordinator_R9703": {
      "title": "WBC Program Coordinator",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-06\nFull time\n\nThe Program Coordinator provides day-to-day coordination and program support for a statewide network of women's business centers serving entrepreneurs, small businesses, and community stakeholders. An entry-level position ideal for someone who is organized, curious, community-minded, and interested in making a meaningful impact through small business support. Working closely with program staff and participating business centers, the Program Coordinator will support events and outreach activities, create social media and newsletter content, assist with client intake and data management, and represent the statewide initiative at community and networking events. The ideal candidate is a self-starter, enjoys working with people, has strong attention to detail, and is excited by the opportunity to learn about entrepreneurship and small business ecosystems across the state. Travel to business centers, events, and partner locations will be required as needed. Responsibilities Include : Provide day-to-day administrative and program support to a statewide network of business centers. Help coordinate communications, deadlines, deliverables, and program activities across multiple locations. Assist with planning, coordinating, and executing workshops, networking events, outreach activities, and other program events. Attend and represent the statewide initiative at events, conferences, workshops, and community activities. Develop and schedule engaging social media content highlighting program activities, success stories, events, resources, and business center initiatives. Gather stories, photos, announcements, and updates from business centers and program partners. Assist with basic graphic design and digital content creation using tools such as Canva. Assist with intake of entrepreneurs and small business clients seeking assistance through the initiative. Help ensure clients receive timely follow-up and appropriate connections to available services. Enter and update information in databases, spreadsheets, CRM systems, or other program tracking tools. Help prepare routine reports, dashboards, and summaries for internal and external stakeholders. Identify missing or inconsistent information and follow up as needed to maintain data quality . Travel to business centers and events throughout the state as needed. Requirements Include : Bachelor's degree in Business Management , Communications , or equivalent preferred. 1-2 years related experience preferred. Equal Opportunity Florida Institute of Technology does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national or ethnic origin, religion, disability, age, genetic information, marital status, citizenship status, veteran status, and other legally protected characteristics in its activities and programs. In accordance with Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Florida Tech does not discriminate on the basis of sex.  Inquiries concerning the application of the Non-Discrimination and Anti-Harassment policy may be directed to the Equal Opportunity Director and Investigator at 150 West University Blvd, Melbourne, FL 32901, or email equalopp@fit.edu , or +1 321-674-7153; or to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Americans with Disabilities Act Please notify us at least five days in advance if a reasonable accommodation for a disability is needed by calling the Office of Human Resources at 321-674-8100. Annual Security & Fire Safety Report The federal Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act (Clery Act) requires colleges and universities, both public and private, participating in federal student aid programs to disclose campus safety information, and imposes certain basic requirements for handling incidents of sexual violence and emergency situations. Florida Tech’s 2026 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report includes statistics for the previous three years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus; in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by Florida Tech; and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from, the campus.   The numbers provided include crime statistics that were reported to local law enforcement agencies, campus security and other Campus Security Authorities.   The report also includes institutional policy statements regarding campus safety and security measures; descriptions of prevention and awareness programs; related university procedures and important guidance; and other essential safety information. You can obtain a printed copy of this report at the Department of Security Welcome Center located at 3126 Panther Place, during normal business hours, or by accessing the following web site 2026 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report . Official Transcripts Official transcripts of all collegiate work must be sent directly from the attended institution to the Office of Human Resources prior to the first day of employment. All international degrees must have a course-by-course official evaluation and translation sent to the Human Resources Office directly from an evaluation company affiliated with the National Association of Credential Evaluation Services, Inc. (NACES). We are an E-verify employer"
    },
    "https://floridatech.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/FloridaTechCareers/job/Emil-Buehler-Center-for-Aviation-Training/Airframe-and-Powerplant--A-P--Mechanic_R9062": {
      "title": "Airframe and Powerplant (A&P) Mechanic",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-13\nFull time\n\nThis position reports to the Shift Supervisor and is responsible for the maintenance and preventive maintenance of the fleet and customer aircraft, components, and equipment, and will be responsible for approving the return to service of fleet and customer aircraft. Responsibilities Include:   Demonstrate the maturity, judgment and analytical ability to perform all aspects of aircraft maintenance and preventive maintenance on fleet and customer aircraft Taxi and run up the aircraft Perform 50/100-hour inspections at required intervals on all fleet and customer aircraft Determine airworthiness of aircraft and components, IAW established procedures and Federal Aviation Regulations May be required to work nights, weekends, or go on A.O.G. trips Assure completeness of all assigned work documents and records, and assist in the cleanup of the maintenance work area Coordinate all activities and complete all work required/assigned by D.O.M. or Shift Supervisor Requirements Include: Education/Special Training/Experience/Requirements: High School graduate or equivalent, or any combination of education and experience that enables one to perform the job functions Must hold a valid Airframe and Powerplant mechanics license Knowledge of Federal Aviation Regulations as they relate to aircraft maintenance Ability to read and interpret aircraft maintenance manuals and specifications to determine feasibility and methods of repairing or replacing malfunctioning or damaged components Must possess all tools Desired Experience: Strong interpersonal and communication skills Proven results-oriented and self-motivated work style Physical and Ergonomic Information and Requirements Must be able to use ladders, work stands, jacks, etc., and be able to work on all areas of the aircraft that may require access during performance of duties. Must be able to lift, carry, or move aircraft components weighing up to 50 lbs. Physical requirements include stooping, kneeling, crouching, crawling, reaching, handling, fingering, and feeling Work is performed in the hangar, flight line, or at remote locations under various weather conditions with elevated noise levels Equal Opportunity Florida Institute of Technology does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national or ethnic origin, religion, disability, age, genetic information, marital status, citizenship status, veteran status, and other legally protected characteristics in its activities and programs. In accordance with Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Florida Tech does not discriminate on the basis of sex.  Inquiries concerning the application of the Non-Discrimination and Anti-Harassment policy may be directed to the Equal Opportunity Director and Investigator at 150 West University Blvd, Melbourne, FL 32901, or email equalopp@fit.edu , or +1 321-674-7153; or to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Americans with Disabilities Act Please notify us at least five days in advance if a reasonable accommodation for a disability is needed by calling the Office of Human Resources at 321-674-8100. Annual Security & Fire Safety Report The federal Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act (Clery Act) requires colleges and universities, both public and private, participating in federal student aid programs to disclose campus safety information, and imposes certain basic requirements for handling incidents of sexual violence and emergency situations. Florida Tech’s 2026 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report includes statistics for the previous three years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus; in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by Florida Tech; and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from, the campus.   The numbers provided include crime statistics that were reported to local law enforcement agencies, campus security and other Campus Security Authorities.   The report also includes institutional policy statements regarding campus safety and security measures; descriptions of prevention and awareness programs; related university procedures and important guidance; and other essential safety information. You can obtain a printed copy of this report at the Department of Security Welcome Center located at 3126 Panther Place, during normal business hours, or by accessing the following web site 2026 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report . Official Transcripts Official transcripts of all collegiate work must be sent directly from the attended institution to the Office of Human Resources prior to the first day of employment. All international degrees must have a course-by-course official evaluation and translation sent to the Human Resources Office directly from an evaluation company affiliated with the National Association of Credential Evaluation Services, Inc. (NACES). We are an E-verify employer"
    },
    "https://floridatech.wd5.myworkdayjobs.com/FloridaTechCareers/job/Emil-Buehler-Center-for-Aviation-Training/Airframe-and-Powerplant--A-P--Mechanic-with-Inspection-Authorization--IA-_R9063": {
      "title": "Airframe and Powerplant (A&P) Mechanic with Inspection Authorization (IA)",
      "description": "Posted: 2026-10-13\nFull time\n\nThis position reports to the Shift Supervisor and is responsible for the maintenance and preventive maintenance of the fleet and customer aircraft, components and equipment and will be responsible for approving the return to service of Annual Inspections, major alterations and repair. Responsibilities Include: Demonstrate the maturity, judgment and analytical ability to perform all aspects of aircraft maintenance and preventive maintenance on fleet and customer aircraft Taxi and run up aircraft Perform 50/100 Hour and Annual Inspections at required intervals on all fleet and customer aircraft Perform major repairs and alterations with completion of Form -337 and STC installation Determine airworthiness of aircraft and components, IAW established procedures and Federal Aviation Regulations May be required to work night, weekends or go on A.O.G. trips Assure completeness of all assigned work documents and records and assist in the cleanup of the maintenance work area Coordinate all activities and complete all work required/assigned by D.O.M. or Shift Supervisor Requirements Include: High School graduate or equivalent, or any combination of education and experience that enables one to perform the job functions Must hold a valid Airframe and Powerplant mechanics license with a current Inspection Authorization endorsement and have adequate training and professional experience Knowledge of Federal Aviation Regulations as they relate to aircraft maintenance Ability to read and interpret aircraft maintenance manuals and specifications to determine feasibility and methods of repairing or replacing malfunctioning or damaged components Must possess all tools Strong interpersonal and communication skills Proven results-oriented and self-motivated work style Physical and Ergonomic Information and Requirements Must be able to use ladders, work stands, jacks, etc. and be able to work on all areas of the aircraft that may require access during performance of duties Must be able to lift, carry, or move aircraft components weighing up to 50 lbs Physical requirements include stooping, kneeling, crouching, crawling, reaching, handling, fingering, and feeling Work is performed in the hangar, flight line or at remote locations under various weather conditions with elevated noise levels Equal Opportunity Florida Institute of Technology does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national or ethnic origin, religion, disability, age, genetic information, marital status, citizenship status, veteran status, and other legally protected characteristics in its activities and programs. In accordance with Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Florida Tech does not discriminate on the basis of sex.  Inquiries concerning the application of the Non-Discrimination and Anti-Harassment policy may be directed to the Equal Opportunity Director and Investigator at 150 West University Blvd, Melbourne, FL 32901, or email equalopp@fit.edu , or +1 321-674-7153; or to the U.S. Department of Education Office for Civil Rights. Americans with Disabilities Act Please notify us at least five days in advance if a reasonable accommodation for a disability is needed by calling the Office of Human Resources at 321-674-8100. Annual Security & Fire Safety Report The federal Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act (Clery Act) requires colleges and universities, both public and private, participating in federal student aid programs to disclose campus safety information, and imposes certain basic requirements for handling incidents of sexual violence and emergency situations. Florida Tech’s 2026 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report includes statistics for the previous three years concerning reported crimes that occurred on campus; in certain off-campus buildings or property owned or controlled by Florida Tech; and on public property within, or immediately adjacent to and accessible from, the campus.   The numbers provided include crime statistics that were reported to local law enforcement agencies, campus security and other Campus Security Authorities.   The report also includes institutional policy statements regarding campus safety and security measures; descriptions of prevention and awareness programs; related university procedures and important guidance; and other essential safety information. You can obtain a printed copy of this report at the Department of Security Welcome Center located at 3126 Panther Place, during normal business hours, or by accessing the following web site 2026 Annual Security and Fire Safety Report . Official Transcripts Official transcripts of all collegiate work must be sent directly from the attended institution to the Office of Human Resources prior to the first day of employment. All international degrees must have a course-by-course official evaluation and translation sent to the Human Resources Office directly from an evaluation company affiliated with the National Association of Credential Evaluation Services, Inc. (NACES). We are an E-verify employer"
